  "exit_criteria": [
    "Explain why volcanoes cluster at subduction zones, rifts and hotspots, and name the melting mechanism that dominates at each",
    "Predict an eruption's likely style from magma composition, temperature, crystal content and volatile content, and justify the prediction as a causal chain",
    "Explain how viscosity controls eruption style, and estimate relative viscosities of basalt, andesite and rhyolite to within orders of magnitude",
    "Classify an eruption on the Volcanic Explosivity Index, and tell apart its products: lava flows, tephra fall, pyroclastic density currents and lahars",
    "Read a volcano's shape and deposit sequence to infer its eruptive history",
    "Interpret basic monitoring signals (earthquake swarms, tremor, inflation or deflation, SO2/CO2 changes) and explain why eruption forecasts are probabilistic",
    "Read a volcanic hazard map, separate hazard from risk, and analyse a historical case study (Pinatubo 1991, Nevado del Ruiz 1985, Tambora 1815) for both its science and its human factors",
    "Explain how large explosive eruptions cool global climate through stratospheric sulfate aerosols, and why the cooling lasts only a few years"
